Description (What we did)-

In this assignment, we built a semantics analyzer using Lex and Yacc.

First, we defined the tokens in our '12340370_12340340.l' file. This file is responsible for scanning the input text and converting it into a stream of tokens that our parser can understand.
Next, in our '12340370_12340340.y'. A crucial part of this was setting the operator precedence and associativity. This ensures that expressions like 'a + b * c' are parsed correctly, with multiplication having a higher precedence than addition.

During coding, we encountered some shift/reduce conflicts which was later resolved with the correct grammar rules and precednce. 

We used the symbol table to insert the identifiers we have seen or morevoer to check wheter they were declared before use or not, we also ensured there is if an dif else statment with proper TAC in outuput, also there is while loop in the code which generates the proper TAC, the input format for the while and if are like that of the C files.
The contents of the array we have used can be accessed by the exression , as the expression can ether evaluate to another array content , or a boolean 0 or 1 , or the expression which evalutes to the number
Earlier extern int was used for debugging.

Compilation:
lex 12340370_12340340.l
yacc -d 12340370_12340340.y
gcc -o 12340370_12340340 lex.yy.c y.tab.c symbol.c

